export anchor AsymmetricFeatureStyle:
    number: 198
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Asymmetric feature
    idea: A 12 column asymmetric grid gives one project the stage, a large navy feature card with a progress ring and its key figures, while a tall watch card, four small project cards, a chart and the activity feed support it at smaller sizes.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f4f4f1, the warm grey behind the cards
        card: #ffffff, cards, the sidebar and fields
        ink: #1c2333, text and figures
        muted: #5b6170, labels, meta and axis text
        navy: #14213d, the feature card, the current nav item and the this week line
        navySoft: #e8ebf2, bar tracks, the this week chart band and initials
        onNavyMuted: #b9c2d6, labels on the feature card
        coral: #c2410c, the New project button and the focus ring
        coralLight: #ffb38a, the ring arc and focus on navy
        series: #6f7fa3, the dashed last week line
        green: #1d7a4a, On track with a solid dot on #e6f4ec
        amber: #8d5000, At risk with a solid triangle on #fdf1dc
        red: #b3261e, Behind with a solid square and overdue on #fdecea
        redOnNavy: #ffb4ab, the outlined Behind tag inside the feature
    type:
        Display figures and headings use Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI
        Variable Display, Segoe UI, system-ui. Text uses system-ui, Segoe
        UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The ring figure is 56px bold at
        minus 0.04em, the greeting 44px bold at minus 0.03em, the feature
        title 36px bold, card figures 26 to 28px bold, body 15px, and
        eyebrows 12px bold caps tracked 0.08em.
    layout:
        A floating white sidebar card with 20px corners holds the brand
        with a navy rounded mark, six nav items with icons where Home is a
        filled navy pill, and Mara Okafor with initials in a coral disc at
        the foot. The main column has a pill search, a round bell and a
        coral pill New project button. Then a 12 column grid with 20px
        gutters. Row one gives 8 columns to the date, a 44px greeting and a
        red clock line for the 4 overdue tasks, and 4 columns to a two by
        two summary card. Row two gives 8 columns to the navy feature card
        for Billing migration, with a Featured project kicker and an
        outlined Behind tag, a 180px coral ring showing 30 percent at left,
        and at right the title, team and due date, a two by two grid of
        tasks done, to go, days left and target pace, a tinted note of the
        latest activity and white and outlined pill buttons. The other 4
        columns hold a tall Also watching card for Mobile app 2.0 with a
        large percent, an amber bar, ruled facts and an outlined Open
        button. Row three is four 3 column cards for the healthy projects,
        each with a status chip, name, team, a large percent, a bar and
        tasks and due. Row four gives 7 columns to an area line chart with
        the this week half on a tinted band and 5 columns to activity.
        Below 1180px the feature and watch cards go full width and project
        cards go two across. On phones the sidebar becomes a top card with
        a scrolling pill nav and everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 28 to 32px inside the feature and 20px gutters.
    density: Low at the top, rising toward the small cards and the feed.
    corners: 20px on the feature and sidebar, 14px on cards, pills for buttons, search and chips, and 12px fields.
    borders: Almost none. 1px warm lines divide the summary cells and the watch facts.
    shadows: A soft lift on cards of 0 1px 2px and 0 8px 24px at low navy. The feature has a deep 0 20px 48px navy shadow.
    icons:
        Round line icons at 1.7px in the sidebar and header. Status chips
        use a solid dot, triangle or square with the word, and overdue uses
        a clock.
    focus: A solid 3px coral outline offset 3px, light coral on the navy feature.
    tone: Editorial and warm, such as Featured project, Also watching and Plan catch-up.
